{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent low bias: forecasts systematically underpredict realized prices by ~2–8 EUR across most horizons; apply an upward level shift, larger when the recent trend is up.",
    "Trend/lag error: the model reacts too slowly to strong upward momentum (breakout regime). Use a momentum overlay: if last 5–10 days are rising, increase the entire path and steepen the first 1–2 weeks.",
    "Horizon-shaped bias: underprediction is largest in the mid-horizon (~day 7–25), while very near-term (day 1–3) errors are smaller. Apply a hump-shaped uplift peaking around week 2–3.",
    "False mean reversion: forecasts revert toward ~72–76 even when the market sustains ~79–84. Suppress mean reversion when price is above recent 30d mean and making higher highs; keep forecasts closer to the prevailing level.",
    "Late-horizon direction mistakes: the model often projects a decline in the last 5–10 days while outcomes stay elevated. Add a floor/anchoring rule: terminal prices should not fall below the recent 10–15d average unless recent returns turn negative."
  ]
}
